{
 "_source": "What a held Control Node lets a Netrunner do with each device on it (Encounter.device_ops / net_device). CPR core p.199: Control takes a Node; each thing on it is worked with its own NET Action, from anywhere in the Architecture while the Node is held, and each Node can be activated once per Turn; Jack Out loses every Node. p.210-211: Control Nodes may be non-combat (cameras, sprinklers, locks, elevators). p.213-216: Defenses; Environmental ones only toggle ON/OFF; Observation Cameras watch a room or corridor and report. Hand-edited; each op's hover card is net_help.json 'dev_<op>'. `bank`: one activation works every device of that type on the Node (HOUSE-RULE, see Encounter.device_ops). `doors`: which doors a seal works (room: the device's own room; gates: the site's gates).",
